$ Goland wing — the Flaps demo model (flaps_env/work/demo/goland.fp), SOL 103 normal modes
$ with the reduced modal model export (MODEXP, #100) that sgear and Flaps read.
$
$ Model: Goland (1945) / Bisplinghoff, Ashley & Halfman (1955) section 9.3, as goland.fp
$ builds it: 13 grids along +y (span 6.096 m), root grid 1 clamped; EI_flap = 9.773e6,
$ EI_chord = 3.0e7, GJ = 9.876e5, EA = 2.0e5 (all N, m; E = G = 1 so PBAR carries the
$ stiffness); 217.74 kg and a torsional inertia of 52.68 kg m^2 spread EQUALLY over grids
$ 1-13 (Flaps conmass node=(1:13)), the C.G. 0.183 m aft of the beam (+x), inertia about
$ the C.G.  That lumping is inferred: it reproduces Flaps 2.3.4's printed coupled modes,
$ 7.370 / 14.119 Hz (flaps_env/docs/demo_results.md), to 4 figures.  Izz = 1.0 kg m^2 is
$ sbeam's (goland.fp gives 0, a massless in-plane rotation); it moves only in-plane modes.
$ EA = 2.0e5 is goland.fp's and gives an axial mode near 3 Hz: pick the flap and torsion
$ modes by shape, not by order.  Units: m, kg, s, N.
$
$ The deck ends with a massless LE/TE outline for animation (#107): see that block.
$ Gates: tests/results/test_modal_export.py (G1 closed form, G2 Flaps, G3, G4, outline).
$
SOL 103
TITLE = Goland wing - Flaps demo model
SET 1 = 1 THRU 13
SUBCASE 1
  SPC    = 1
  METHOD = 1
  MODEXP(OP4,UF) = 1
